---
description: General engineering principles for ost-linker
alwaysApply: true
---

# General

- No untested code when testing is feasible. If tests or lint fail, fix and re-run until green.
- KISS over clever abstractions. Comments only when the signature is not enough.
- English only in code, comments, logs, and docs.
- No emojis in logs or comments.
- API layer must run self-contained (Postgres + env only); pipeline external calls are optional and mockable in tests.

# Git

- Branch from `develop`. Never commit on `develop` / `main` / `staging`.
- Do not merge to those branches; open a PR and stop.
- Conventional Commits (`feat`, `fix`, `chore`, …). Author: `spideystreet <dhicham.pro@gmail.com>`.
- No AI attribution in commits or PRs. Tag/version only for an actual release.
